Additional Terms for InternMailing:

1. ACADEMIC AND PROFESSIONAL USE
This software is designed for legitimate academic research outreach and 
professional networking purposes. Users are expected to:
- Respect email recipients and anti-spam laws
- Follow university and institutional policies
- Use the system responsibly and ethically

2. NO WARRANTY FOR EMAIL DELIVERY
While the system is designed to maximize email delivery success, the authors
make no guarantee regarding email delivery rates, response rates, or outcomes.

3. USER RESPONSIBILITY
Users are responsible for:
- Compliance with local laws and regulations (CAN-SPAM, GDPR, etc.)
- Maintaining appropriate professional communication standards
- Respecting recipient privacy and opt-out requests

4. ATTRIBUTION
If you use this software in academic research or professional settings,
attribution to the InternMailing project is appreciated but not required.

5. COMMERCIAL USE
Commercial use is permitted under this license, but users should ensure
compliance with applicable laws and regulations for commercial email practices.

For questions about licensing or usage, please create an issue on the
GitHub repository: https://github.com/Flamechargerr/InternMailing